::ENG4_U03_L01_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG4.R.05] Passage: A city report first explains that sidewalks near schools are unsafe, then lists crash data, then recommends wider sidewalks and better lighting. What structure does the passage use most clearly? {
~A. Chronological narrative#The passage is not telling events in time order.
=B. Problem-solution#Correct. It presents a safety problem and recommends solutions.
~C. Literary flashback#The passage is informational, not literary.
~D. Personal reflection#The passage focuses on public planning, not personal thought.
}
::ENG4_U03_L01_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG4.R.05] Passage: A city report first explains that sidewalks near schools are unsafe, then lists crash data, then recommends wider sidewalks and better lighting. Which feature would most improve effectiveness? {
=A. A map showing school zones with the highest risk#Correct. A map would help readers connect the recommendation to locations.
~B. A poem about walking#This would not directly support the report's purpose.
~C. A random photo of a park#A random image would not clarify the sidewalk issue.
~D. A list of unrelated city holidays#This would distract from the problem.
}
::ENG4_U03_L01_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: Reflective roofs can reduce building heat by sending more sunlight away from the surface. Which paraphrase is accurate? {
~A. Reflective roofs create more heat by trapping sunlight.#This reverses the meaning.
~B. Reflective roofs work only at night.#The passage does not say this.
=C. Reflective roofs help lower heat because they send sunlight away from buildings.#Correct. This preserves the cause-effect relationship.
~D. Reflective roofs replace all city trees.#This is not stated.
}
::ENG4_U03_L01_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: A flexible system can improve efficiency without excluding patients who need additional support. What does efficiency mean here? {
~A. Confusion#This is the opposite of the meaning.
~B. Decoration#This is unrelated.
~C. Delay#This is the opposite of efficient work.
=D. Completing tasks with less wasted time or effort#Correct. Efficiency means working effectively with less waste.
}
::ENG4_U03_L01_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG4.L.01] Passage: Text features help readers understand complex information. Which sentence follows standard conventions? {
=A. Headings, charts, and transitions can guide readers through complex information.#Correct. The series and verb agreement are clear.
~B. Headings charts and transitions can guide readers through complex information.#Commas are needed in the series.
~C. Headings, charts, and transitions guides readers through complex information.#The verb should be guide.
~D. headings, charts, and transitions can guide readers through complex information.#The sentence should begin with a capital letter.
}
